#{[17592186420909 "![](images/65/653699a9c78577272425de7f8e6d015743e2c2e8c6e9a21bef189dc06fd80684.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{5}{y}^{7}\\,i+x{y}^{3}\\,j$ and the rectangle $C$ shown above. If the flux of $F$ across the side ${C}_{1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186420910 "![](images/28/28a7eb32cfcd800c907e9f4af927eca7bd8616d36162682413db62a9feabefbb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186420911 "![](images/01/01d8d85064253b9241b1fd93c22381897f23556d6e02c5c2c0161c94cee3bbdf.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186420912 "![](images/af/afaec113101f1a63134d2b1cb5c9744b93f9b84dabafaa205780d2dc5b49a7bc.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186420913 "![](images/1b/1b08e4cc9dd6ebde7f4bf544d7a76c4706dbd69a2c31d4c0fda8f816d4f871b5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)=(x+y)^{2}\\,i+(x-y)^{2}\\,j$ and the rectangle $C$  shown above. If the flux of $F$ across the side ${C}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186420914 "![](images/0f/0f1d25942ae680c068b587f38bfbc968c8850b8fa2db2003e994e1ec32dad892.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186420915 "![](images/f4/f413fd04759cdb02118b320fea2f678712681a57f5b08e1bcb57a6843c0c80f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=4x\\,i+4y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $6$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across all four sides of the square.*"] [17592186420916 "![](images/9d/9da6bdb9ab5f93d0b0d11dfd60ab2b647380a94ce337c2314ec3504cabafa889.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=4x\\,i-3y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $2$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across the vertical sides, and similarly for the horizontal sides.*"] [17592186420917 "![](images/57/575463a6fbe18d3f9b805e1a9c3d8e52bedd84a8db3a3c90d87381b8cb7abf74.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=-4x\\,i-4y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $2$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across all four sides of the square.*"] [17592186421470 "![](images/95/958965484cd271c5eb7ccfc8bf913386e57b9b733719885d232e562063969ca8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=-x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $4$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across the vertical sides, and similarly for the horizontal sides.*"] [17592186421783 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,xy,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$"] [17592186421784 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3uv,\\,u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.$*"] [17592186421785 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$"] [17592186424178 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=v+w,\\,y=u+w,\\,z=u+v.\n$$"] [17592186424179 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=au,\\,y=bv,\\,z=cw.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $a$, $b$ and $c$ are fixed constants."] [17592186424180 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u}+v \\\\ v+w \\\\ vw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186424181 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{z}{y} \\\\ y \\\\ xz\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$\n\n*Hint: You can assume that $y,z\\ne 0.$*"] [17592186424182 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)),$ given that \n\n$$\nu=x,\\,v=2y,\\,w=3z.\n$$"] [17592186424621 "![](images/4d/4d4c2c86ed8506ff034141ac20a5a56587a80370384ceeaf08c66f2ce3e8a315.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y=-\\sqrt{x}$ from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(4,-2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(4,-2)$ to the point $B(4,0).$\n\nGiven that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{8}{3},\n$$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [17592186424622 "Let $F(x,y,z)={e}^{y+z}\\,i+{e}^{x+z}\\,j+{e}^{x+y}\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?\n$$"] [17592186431183 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+2\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2).$"] [17592186431184 "Use Stokes' theorem to evaluate \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\text{curl}\\,F=⟨x+y,\\,-x+y,\\,-2z⟩,$ and $C$ is the intersection of the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and the paraboloid $z=(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}.$ The curve $C$ is oriented counter-clockwise when viewed from above."] [17592186431185 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+({t}^{2}-{t}^{3})\\,j+({t}^{2}-t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$\nGiven that $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+3y\\,k,$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$"] [17592186431186 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $r(t)=(2{t}^{3}-2t)\\,i+(t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(-t-{t}^{2})\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,0).$\nGiven that $F(x,y,z)=y\\,i+x\\,k,$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$"] [17592186431187 "Let $C$ be the intersection of the half-cone $z=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and the boundary of the infinite vertical column enclosed by the planes $y=1+x,$ $x=0,$ and $y=0.$ Given that the curve $C$ is oriented counter-clockwise when viewed from above and $\\text{curl}\\,F=⟨0,\\,-{z}^{3},\\,0⟩,$ the circulation of $F$ along $C$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr=\n$$"] [17592186431188 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=z\\,j-y\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1)$"] [17592186434830 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$"] [17592186434831 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.$*"] [17592186436123 "Find  $\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+xz+xy+yz}{x+z}.$"] [17592186436124 "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (3,-3,2)}\\,\\frac{zx+zy}{\\sqrt{x+y+4}-2}=\n$$"] [17592186436125 "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{x(xy-1)}{y}.$"] [17592186436126 "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (-2,-2)}\\sqrt{xy}.$"] [17592186436127 "Determine $\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}.$"] [17592186436128 "Determine $\\lim_{x\\to (1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{x+y}.$"] [17592186436129 "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (4,-4,-2)}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x-y}}{z}=\n$$"] [17592186436130 "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{\\sqrt{6+y}-x}{6+y-{x}^{2}}=\n$$"] [17592186437020 "Given $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$"] [17592186437021 "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [17592186447371 "At which point on the curve ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=xy$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$"] [17592186447374 "At which point on the curve $x{y}^{2}=3-2y$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$"] [17592186459235 "At which points on the curve $2xy=2x-y$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $2\\,i-j?$"] [17592186475943 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,2)}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nI. The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=2$\n\nII. The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2}$ along the path $y=x+1$\n\nIII. The limit does not exist"] [17592186480656 "Suppose $|\\,c\\,|=6\\sqrt{3}$ and the angle between vectors $c$ and $d$ is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$"] [17592186480689 "Suppose $|\\,a\\,|=7$ and the angle between vectors $a$ and $b$ is $\\theta ={90}^{∘}.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186488225 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+2x\\ge 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-2x\\ne 1\\}$"] [17592186490212 "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\right)i+\\left(\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}\\right)j\n$$ over the domain $D=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>{x}^{2}\\}.$"] [17592186490290 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT(\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix})⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n  \n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [17592186490314 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j$"] [17592186490318 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-xy\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,i+({y}^{2}-2xy)\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,i-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y)\\,j$"] [17592186499455 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}+4y)\\,i-(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y)\\,j$"] [17592186499504 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j?$"] [17592186499510 "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=(x-1)i-y\\,j$ over the domain $D={R}^{2}.$"] [17592186499527 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}-xy=x+1$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$"] [17592186499535 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)=({y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y)\\,i+({x}^{3}+3x{y}^{2})\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=2x\\,i+4{y}^{4}\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=(x+y)\\,i-3y\\,j$"] [17592186499564 "![](images/9f/9f2f77c6c2047dcd3f542fc0f640a68b45a4d40784d0e7eaacdcadb002c79de5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following shows the streamlines of this vector field?"] [17592186500338 "At which points on the curve $3y{x}^{2}=48+3x{y}^{2}$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i-j?$"] [17592186501152 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,\\,-2y,\\,-z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{3},\\,{v}^{3},\\,uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n